---
// biome-ignore lint/correctness/noUnusedImports: used in the template below the frontmatter fence, which Biome does not parse for .astro files
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Disclaimer — APIs">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100">
    Disclaimer
  </h1>
  <div class="mt-6 flex flex-col gap-8 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
    <section aria-labelledby="independence-heading">
      <h2
        id="independence-heading"
        class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"
      >
        1. Independence and trademarks
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This site is an independent hobby project listing APIs I maintain
        myself. It isn't affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by GitHub or
        the Go module proxy (pkg.go.dev) — any product names, logos, and brands
        mentioned are the property of their respective owners.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="source-heading">
      <h2
        id="source-heading"
        class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"
      >
        2. Source of truth
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        The links here (repos, OpenAPI specs, SDK docs) point at the actual
        source of truth for each API and are kept up to date on a best-effort
        basis, but this page itself can lag the repos it links to — the repo is
        always the authority, not this catalogue.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-3 list-disc pl-5">
        <li>
          <strong>Repositories:</strong> each API's and SDK's own repo on
          github.com/alrayyes.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>OpenAPI specs:</strong> the spec file in each API's repo.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>SDK docs:</strong> each SDK's own docs site, or pkg.go.dev for
          Go.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="warranty-heading">
      <h2
        id="warranty-heading"
        class="text-lg font-semibold tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100"
      >
        3. Warranty and liability
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-2">
        This software is provided as-is, without warranty of any kind, per the
        terms of the
        <a
          href="/license"
          class="text-accent underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-accent-hover dark:text-accent-dark dark:hover:text-accent-dark-hover"
        >
          GPL-3.0-or-later
        </a>
        licence it's distributed under.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
